Chapter: HdaAudioTest
  cites Kernel chapter HdaAudio

 hda-square-tone 480 200 builds a 48 kHz square wave at 480 Hz: the
 period is 48000/480 = 100 samples, high for the first 50 and low for
 the rest. Each 16-bit signed sample is written little-endian into both
 stereo channels: the high level +8000 is 0x1F40 (lo 64, hi 31), the low
 level -8000 is 0xE0C0 (lo 192, hi 224). So sample 0 (high) is the four
 bytes 64,31,64,31 and sample 60 (past the half-period, low) begins
 192,224 at byte offset 240.

Section: Body

  check : Integer -> Text
  check (x) =
    let buf = hda-square-tone 480 200
    in if peek-byte buf 0 /= 64 then "FAIL: sample 0 left low byte"
    else if peek-byte buf 1 /= 31 then "FAIL: sample 0 left high byte"
    else if peek-byte buf 2 /= 64 then "FAIL: sample 0 right channel not mirrored"
    else if peek-byte buf 3 /= 31 then "FAIL: sample 0 right high byte"
    else if peek-byte buf 240 /= 192 then "FAIL: sample 60 not low level"
    else if peek-byte buf 241 /= 224 then "FAIL: sample 60 low high byte"
    else "PASS"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (check 0)
  end
